Z||000001||1FST2M6||12-08-2000||11:47 AM||||in my (former) fiero  13.6@103  on nitrous... 40hp shot<P>fastest ever..  '79 Corvette 12.86@121   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>BBAD GT runs better then that in a daily driven Mustang!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Eric_PA||12-09-2000||10:45 AM||||Ok, i never had actuall Quarter mile times for my Fiero yet but did use a G-tech pro. I was getting consistant 16.7 second quarter mile runs on it. Then I decided to use it on my Sunfire, I got a few 15.29's at 95MPH and a couple 15.44's at about the same speed. I figured this was way too good to be true. I decided to take the Sunfire to the track and run it. Wasn't too bad. I got 15.782 at 87.5 which is better than stock, so it shows that the mods I made did something. I should have taken the Fiero to get a before time before i do an engine swap.<P>moral of the story, it seems that the G-tech pro's are about .5sec. optomistic. So would that mean that my automatic GT would have ran a 17 second quarter mile. Does that sound right?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||hugh||12-09-2000||06:51 PM||||12.20@115 in my 87 Grand National<BR>10.13@131 in my dragster(hurt engine melted 3 of 6 pistons)||||reg||1
Z||000004||L.I. Fieros||12-09-2000||07:12 PM||||86 SE -- 4 spd. -- 15.95 @ 89.1 mph using a G-Tech.  The mph with a G-Tech will always be higher than at the track because it is giving the speed at the exact end of the 1/4 mile.  At the track it is your average speed over the last 60 ft. I believe.||||reg||6
Z||000005||BBBAD GT||12-09-2000||07:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by hugh:<BR><B>10.13@131 in my dragster(hurt engine melted 3 of 6 pistons)</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Don't you hate it when your best time is normally when you break stuff?  Lean is mean.......||||reg||1
Z||000006||hugh||12-10-2000||07:21 PM||||I was making licensing runs,that was my 3rd of 6 I had to make.They have to get progressively faster.The car has the potential to go around 165/170 @somewhere around mid 8's.Not bad for 274 cubic inches!someday I may get around to getting the dragster back together again.By the way,It cost me $4400 to fix the engine.||||reg||1
Z||000007||HYPTNOTiSE||12-11-2000||02:28 AM||||When my fiero was completely stock except for a short shifter, and K&N airfilter i ran a 16.01 at 75-80 dragway.  It was during the day with my v-6 4 speed combo in my 86GT.  <P>My 89 S-10 ran a 17.80's at the track. It was a blast, it doesn't matter what you run, it's all so much fun.  4cyl 5 speed, i even beat a v-6 ranger, that felt good, he had traction problems he said. <P>Can't wait! I'll have all winter to tune my new 3.2/3.83 5 speed combo. I should have some awesome timeslips this spring for you guys! I may even start spraying it again by that time!<P>||||reg||1
